1882..1956 Comment "/// A path at every loop whose inverse arm drops its rest\'s path: each arm"
1957..2038 Comment "/// checks at its letter, but at `loop ∷ back(loop) ∷ q` the loop arm carries"
2039..2119 Comment "/// the inverse arm\'s reflexivity to `here(loop ∷ back(loop) ∷ q)`, which is"
2120..2195 Comment "/// not the path at `q` the cancellation\'s right side reads. Read as a set,"
2196..2264 Comment "/// the loops would identify the two; the words are not read as one."
